  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Phy 304.02 Materials Required to Accompany the License Application Form. At the time that applicants for initial licensure submit their completed license application form, they shall submit the “Addendum to the Universal Application for Initial License - Physical Therapists and Physical Therapy Assistants” revised 4/2026, mark the box for the license type the applicant is applying for, either “Physical Therapist” or “Physical Therapy Assistant”, and attest that:\n\n(a) If the applicant is required by Phy 306.04 to take and pass a test of English language proficiency, the applicant’s examination scores have been sent directly to the office of professional licensure and certification (OPLC) by the Educational Testing Service;\n\n(b) The applicant’s examination scores have been sent directly to the OPLC by FSBPT; and\n\n(c) The passing scores on the jurisprudence assessment module have been sent directly to the OPLC by the FSBPT.\n\nSource. #9233, eff 8-22-08; ss by #9429, eff 3-19-09; ss by #9653, eff 2-5-10; ss by #9869, eff 2-18-11; ss by #10060, eff 12-23-11; ss by #10401, eff 8-23-13; ss by #10724, eff 11-22-14; ss by #12864, eff 9-10-19 (formerly Phy 304.04); ss by #14563, eff 6-20-26, EXPIRES: 6-20-36\n\nREVISION NOTE:\n\nDocument #14563, effective 6-20-26, repealed Part Phy 305.02 through Phy 305.05 in Chapter Phy 300, titled “Issuance of Full Initial Licenses”, “Issuance of Conditional Licenses”, “Demonstration of Continuing Competence by Those Applying 12 or More Months After Passing the Examination”, and “Demonstration of Continuing Competence by Those Applying for Initial Licensure 12 or More Months After Passing the Applicable National Examination When Not Active in the Profession”.\n\nDocument #14563, effective 6-20-26, repealed Part Phy 309.02 through Phy 309.04 in Chapter Phy 300, titled “Restriction on Temporary Licenses”, “Basic Eligibility Requirements for Temporary Licenses”, and “Issuance and Expiration of Temporary Licenses”.",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/phy300.html"
}
